## v1.1 amendment — Documentation Sync (2026-05-20)

**Trigger:** Boz request — "ensure documents are always updated to reflect any changes made"

The four engineering rules above are now joined by a fifth standing rule, mirrored canonically in the project-level `.claude/CLAUDE.md` under the **Documentation Sync (Mandatory)** section.

### Rule 5 — Same-session doc sync

Every change Cove makes to system state — code, config, infrastructure, secrets, groups, projects, schemas, dependencies, deployments, runbooks — MUST be reflected in the documentation that describes it, in the **same session as the change**. Documentation is not a follow-up; it is part of the change.

**What counts as documentation** (see project [CLAUDE.md](http://CLAUDE.md) for the full list): repo READMEs and component docs, all `CLAUDE.md` files, ClickUp governance docs and tickets, auto-memory files, `anvil_registry` metadata, scratch backlogs referenced by open tickets.

**Same-session exception:** If a doc cannot be updated in the current session (system locked, third-party tool unreachable, etc.), Cove MUST create a follow-up ClickUp task in `00-INTAKE` immediately and flag it in the Delta Summary — not next session, not "later".

**Reporting:** Every Delta Summary lists the docs touched alongside the substantive change. A change with no doc touched must explicitly justify why (typically only pure read-only ops).

**Prohibited:**

*   "I'll document it later"
*   Updating code without updating the runbook (or vice versa)
*   Letting [CLAUDE.md](http://CLAUDE.md) drift behind repo state
*   Stale memory references after the underlying resource has moved/changed
*   Marking a task complete when its docs haven't been updated

### Canonical source

The project-level `.claude/CLAUDE.md` in the ANVIL repo holds the authoritative version of this rule. This ClickUp doc mirrors it for cross-surface visibility (Cowork, Chat, ad-hoc sessions). If the two diverge, the repo wins — repo is checked into git and loaded into every coding session automatically.

